{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QzoBEdMwPf92z8LBFjB8N5","type":"tool_result","content":"752\t**4.** A `RoleBinding` in namespace `web` grants a `ClusterRole` called `pod-reader` to a ServiceAccount. A second `ClusterRoleBinding` grants the same `ClusterRole` to the same ServiceAccount. What can the ServiceAccount read?\n753\t\n754\tA) Pods in `web` only — the RoleBinding constrains the ClusterRoleBinding\n755\tB) Pods cluster-wide\n756\tC) Nothing — the two bindings conflict and RBAC resolves conflicts by denying\n757\tD) Pods in `web`, plus Pods in the ServiceAccount's own namespace\n758\t\n759\t---\n760\t\n761\t**5.** An application deployed via Helm has been upgraded three times. A bad configuration shipped in the third upgrade. The team wants the previous state of *all* objects the chart manages. Which is correct?\n762\t\n763\tA) `kubectl rollout undo` on the Deployment\n764\tB) `helm rollback <release> 2`\n765\tC) `kubectl apply` the previous manifests from `templates/`\n766\tD) Delete the release and reinstall the chart at the previous chart version\n767\t\n768\t---\n769\t\n770\t**6.** A PersistentVolume with `persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy: Retain` had its bound PVC deleted. A new PVC with identical requirements is created and stays `Pending`. Why?\n771\t\n772\tA) `Retain` volumes can only be bound once, ever\n773\tB) The PV is in `Released`, not `Available` — the previous claimant's data remains and an administrator must reclaim it manually\n774\tC) The new PVC needs `volumeName` set explicitly\n775\tD) `Retain` requires the DefaultStorageClass admission plugin to be disabled\n776\t\n777\t---\n778\t\n779\t**7.** A team runs an Argo CD instance that watches a Git repository and applies manifests to the cluster. Which statement correctly describes the security property this delivery model provides?"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"162e0c3b-d249-45ca-887d-880c72b06ba7","uuid":"5a66e1f2-6a8d-4798-9ee0-a70229df56bf","timestamp":"2026-08-31T22:58:40.660Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/.pipeline-state/ch-19/draft-v1.md","content":"**4.** A `RoleBinding` in namespace `web` grants a `ClusterRole` called `pod-reader` to a ServiceAccount. A second `ClusterRoleBinding` grants the same `ClusterRole` to the same ServiceAccount. What can the ServiceAccount read?\n\nA) Pods in `web` only — the RoleBinding constrains the ClusterRoleBinding\nB) Pods cluster-wide\nC) Nothing — the two bindings conflict and RBAC resolves conflicts by denying\nD) Pods in `web`, plus Pods in the ServiceAccount's own namespace\n\n---\n\n**5.** An application deployed via Helm has been upgraded three times. A bad configuration shipped in the third upgrade. The team wants the previous state of *all* objects the chart manages. Which is correct?\n\nA) `kubectl rollout undo` on the Deployment\nB) `helm rollback <release> 2`\nC) `kubectl apply` the previous manifests from `templates/`\nD) Delete the release and reinstall the chart at the previous chart version\n\n---\n\n**6.** A PersistentVolume with `persistentVolumeReclaimPolicy: Retain` had its bound PVC deleted. A new PVC with identical requirements is created and stays `Pending`. Why?\n\nA) `Retain` volumes can only be bound once, ever\nB) The PV is in `Released`, not `Available` — the previous claimant's data remains and an administrator must reclaim it manually\nC) The new PVC needs `volumeName` set explicitly\nD) `Retain` requires the DefaultStorageClass admission plugin to be disabled\n\n---\n\n**7.** A team runs an Argo CD instance that watches a Git repository and applies manifests to the cluster. Which statement correctly describes the security property this delivery model provides?","numLines":28,"startLine":752,"totalLines":940}}}
